From: esp32-firmware <info@tinkerforge.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Only forward traffic through NAPT interfaces

Enabling IP_FORWARD for optional Ethernet sharing must not turn the device
into a router while sharing is disabled. ip4_forward only calls
ip_napt_forward when the output interface does not have NAPT enabled.
Reject forwarding if the input interface does not have NAPT enabled either.

---
 src/core/ipv4/ip4_napt.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/core/ipv4/ip4_napt.c b/src/core/ipv4/ip4_napt.c
--- a/src/core/ipv4/ip4_napt.c
+++ b/src/core/ipv4/ip4_napt.c
@@ -868,6 +868,8 @@
 err_t
 ip_napt_forward(struct pbuf *p, struct ip_hdr *iphdr, struct netif *inp, struct netif *outp)
 {
+  /* The output interface is not a NAPT interface. Only forward traffic
+     arriving from a NAPT interface, keeping routing opt-in at runtime. */
   if (!inp->napt)
-    return ERR_OK;
+    return ERR_RTE;
 
